# Baseline captured 2026-11-26 by scanning the five images
# `docker compose -f infrastructure/compose/docker-compose.yml config --images` lists today
# (postgres:16-alpine, mongo:7, redis:7-alpine, rabbitmq:3-management-alpine,
# nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.27-alpine) with `trivy image --severity CRITICAL,HIGH`.
#
# Every entry below already has a "fixed version" per Trivy's own metadata -- that only
# means the upstream package maintainer (Alpine, Go, npm) has published a patch; none of
# these five vendor images have been rebuilt on top of that patch yet, and we don't control
# when they are. There is nothing to change on our side today.
#
# This file is a living baseline, not a one-time waiver: whenever Renovate opens a PR
# bumping one of these image tags/digests, this workflow re-scans the new build and any
# entry below that no longer appears should be deleted in that same PR. A CVE ID that
# reappears after being removed, or a severity bump on an existing one, is a signal worth
# re-reading before re-adding it blindly.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# usr/local/bin/gosu (privilege-drop helper bundled by the official postgres and mongo
# images) is a statically-linked Go binary built against an older Go toolchain. These are
# Go stdlib CVEs disclosed against that toolchain; gosu's upstream maintainer has not
# published a build against a patched Go release, so postgres/mongo can't rebuild on top of
# one either. Tracked upstream: https://github.com/tianon/gosu.
#
# The same CVE IDs also show up against the Go stdlib embedded in the statically-linked
# grafana and mongodb_exporter binaries (Task #92/Phase 4) -- same root cause (project
# hasn't republished against a newer Go toolchain yet), different vendor.
# Affects: postgres:16-alpine, mongo:7, grafana/grafana:13.3.2, percona/mongodb_exporter:0.54.0
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2025-61726
CVE-2025-61729
CVE-2025-68121
CVE-2026-111943
CVE-2026-25679
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-32280
CVE-2026-32281
CVE-2026-32283
CVE-2026-33811
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39820
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-39822
CVE-2026-39836
CVE-2026-42499
CVE-2026-42504
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# golang.org/x/net, vendored into the statically-linked mongo CLI tool binaries
# (bsondump, mongodump, mongoexport, mongofiles, mongoimport, mongorestore, mongostat,
# mongotop). Same situation as gosu above: fixed upstream in x/net, not yet in a republished
# mongo image build.
#
# Also present in grafana, prometheus, and mongodb_exporter's own vendored x/net (Task #92/
# Phase 4) at their current latest release -- same situation, different vendor.
# Affects: mongo:7, grafana/grafana:13.3.2, prom/prometheus:v3.16.0,
#   percona/mongodb_exporter:0.54.0
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-78661

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# js-yaml, bundled with the Node.js-based mongosh shipped in the mongo image. Fixed upstream
# in js-yaml; not yet pulled into a republished mongo image build.
# Affects: mongo:7
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-59869
CVE-2026-84375
GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj

